<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Winston County, Mississippi</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Winston County is a county in east-central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, with its seat at Louisville. It was formed in 1833 from land ceded by the Choctaw in the Treaty of Dancing Rabbit Creek and named after Louis Winston, an early Mississippi official. It contains <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nanih-waiya">Nanih Waiya</a>, the great mound regarded by the Choctaw as their place of origin.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/winston-county-mississippi.jpg" alt="Winston County, Mississippi" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kaldari · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Strand_Theatre_Louisville.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
